Execution 009 - direct resident-slot expert compute (LLAMA_MOE_PAGING_COMPUTE_MODE=direct_sparse).

Selected experts stay in their M resident-cache slots; the CPU MUL_MAT_ID consumes the
K=8 selected slots directly with zero K8 expert-weight materialization. A runtime hook
lets llama-moe-paging serve MUL_MAT_ID before the generic CPU implementation runs.
Adds a direct_dense control mode (resident slots, ordinary MUL_MAT_ID, no hook).

Execution 011 adds unambiguous direct counters: direct_calls (paging slot events),
direct_mul_mat_id_calls (hook ops, once per op), direct_selected_matrices (== calls*K)
and paging_layer_events. They show the hook runs only at ngl=0 and never at ngl=99.

Correction (Execution 011): the 009 exactness evidence was taken at -ngl 99, where
direct_mul_mat_id_calls == 0 and Metal computed from the resident slots. It did not
validate this CPU hook. At ngl=0 direct_dense (resident slots + ordinary MUL_MAT_ID)
is token-identical to staging, but direct_sparse is numerically incorrect. See
executions/011-RESULT.md and results/exec011_exactness_diagnosis.md.

